<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"about-intro" aria-labelledby=3D"about-=
intro-title"><h1 id=3D"about-intro-title">Introduction</h1><p class=3D"gb-l=
ede">Material web, also known as Material Web Components or MWC, is a libra=
ry of web components that follows Google's Material Design guidelines.</p><=
p class=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/a=
bout/intro/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/about/intro/</a></p><div class=3D=
"gb-content"><div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-intro--what-is-material" tabindex=3D"-1">What is Material?<=
/h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-intro--what-is-material"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhat is Material?=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Material Design is a design system built and supported by Google designe=
rs and
developers. Guidelines for building Material apps and components are publis=
hed
on <a href=3D"https://material.io">material.io</a>.</p>
<p>Version 3.0 implements <strong>Material 3 Expressive</strong>, the lates=
t evolution of
Material 3: a larger shape scale with shape morphing, spring-based motion, =
an
emphasized type scale, and an updated dynamic color system. The elements ar=
e
named <code>md-gb-*</code>, follow the
<a href=3D"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.3/">WAI-ARIA</a> patterns for t=
heir roles, and
only rely on web platform features that are
<a href=3D"https://web.dev/baseline">Baseline</a> widely available (newer f=
eatures are
guarded and degrade gracefully).</p>
<p><img src=3D"/about/images/what-is-material.webp" alt=3D"An example of a =
Material Design application." title=3D"What is Material?"></p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-intro--what-are-web-components" tabindex=3D"-1">What are we=
b components?</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-intro--what-are-web-components"><span cl=
ass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhat are web components?=E2=80=9D</span>=
 <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p><a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_componen=
ts">Web components</a>
are custom HTML elements with encapsulated styles and behavior. They work a=
cross
many different frameworks (such as Lit, React, Vue, and Svelte) as well as =
web
environments (such as Eleventy, Wordpress, and Ruby on Rails).</p>
<p>Many components in this library are drop-in replacements for browser ele=
ments
like <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>. Every elem=
ent is prefixed with <code>md-gb-</code>.</p>
