dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Two central suites render rows in <code>labs/gb/components/shared/centra=
l</code> and run in a real browser:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>axe</strong> (<code>axe_test.ts</code>): axe-core with no rule =
disabled, on every subject of
the central table (<code>subjects.ts</code>) plus 29 overlay rows in their
open state (<code>axe-helpers.ts</code>).</li>
<li><strong>ARIA 1.3</strong> (<code>aria_test.ts</code>): the axe rows plu=
s 34 rows that put
components in the states ARIA depends on (selected, checked, expanded,
grouped, with panels, with an error), checked against the WAI-ARIA 1.3 role
and attribute rules. 27 rows are open overlays, so the checks that
flip state skip them.</li>
</ul>
<p>Known gaps are rows with a real violation. They move to <code>axe_gap.ts=
</code> and
<code>aria_gap.ts</code> (red on purpose) and are recorded in <code>AXE_GAP=
S</code> and
<code>ARIA_GAPS</code>. Today: axe none; ARIA none.
Suite files: <code>aria_gap.ts</code>, <code>aria_test.ts</code>, <code>axe=
_gap.ts</code>, <code>axe_test.ts</code>.</p>
