">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>npm run gb:baseline</code> maps every CSS feature in the compiled =
<code>labs/gb</code> CSS
to its web-features Baseline status. A feature that is not widely available
must sit inside a matching <code>@supports</code> guard or be listed with a=
 reason in
<code>scripts/gb-baseline-allow.json</code>; anything else fails the run.</=
p>
<ul>
<li>CSS: 19,541 feature uses in 62 files; 51 features are not widely availa=
ble, used 754 times (478 guarded, 276 allowed with a reason, <strong>0 ungu=
arded</strong>). Result: passes.</li>
<li>JavaScript (report only): 31 tracked Web API members in 207 source file=
s; 6 are not widely available, 3 of them with at least one use that is not =
feature-detected.</li>
</ul>
