<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"about-support--why-doesn't-prefers-color-scheme:-dark-switch-the-=
theme" tabindex=3D"-1">Why doesn't <code>prefers-color-scheme: dark</code> =
switch the theme?</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-support--why-doesn't-prefers-color-schem=
e:-dark-switch-the-theme"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhy do=
esn't prefers-color-scheme: dark switch the theme?=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The tokens use <code>light-dark()</code>, so they follow the <code>color=
-scheme</code> property. Set
it to follow the system, or force a scheme on any subtree.</p>
<figure class=3D"gb-demo" aria-label=3D"A subtree that is always dark" id=
=3D"gbd-4d73c6">
