an class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CCheck your own app=E2=80=9D</span> =
<span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Test on the oldest version of each browser in the table, not only the cu=
rrent
release. To see which Baseline features the repository uses, run
<code>npm run gb:baseline</code>.</p>
</div></section>
<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"about-ai-agents" aria-labelledby=3D"ab=
out-ai-agents-title"><h1 id=3D"about-ai-agents-title">AI agents</h1><p clas=
s=3D"gb-lede">labs/gb/skill/ is a Claude Code skill named md-gb.</p><p clas=
s=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/about/a=
i-agents/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/about/ai-agents/</a></p><div class=
=3D"gb-content"><div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-ai-agents--what-the-skill-is" tabindex=3D"-1">What the skil=
l is</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-ai-agents--what-the-skill-is"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhat the skill is=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>labs/gb/skill/</code> is a Claude Code skill named <code>md-gb</co=
de>. It teaches an agent which
<code>md-gb-*</code> element to pick, and each element's attributes, proper=
ties, slots,
events, CSS parts, custom properties, and what the app must provide itself.=
 It
is one <code>SKILL.md</code> plus a reference file per component.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-ai-agents--install-it" tabindex=3D"-1">Install it</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-ai-agents--install-it"><span class=3D"of=
fscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CInstall it=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"t=
rue">#</span></a></div>
<p>Copy the folder into your skills directory. For all of your projects:</p=
>

<lit-island import=3D"/js/hydration-entrypoints/copy-code-button.js" on:int=
eraction=3D"focusin,pointerenter,touchstart">
  <div class=3D"gb-code"><pre class=3D"language-sh" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"=
region" aria-label=3D"Code 26"><code class=3D"language-sh"><span class=3D"t=
oken function">mkdir</span> <span class=3D"token parameter variable">-p</sp=
an> ~/.claude/skills/md-gb
<span class=3D"token function">cp</span> <span class=3D"token parameter var=
iable">-r</span> labs/gb/skill/. ~/.claude/skills/md-gb/</code></pre></div>
</lit-island>
<p>To share it with one repository, copy it to <code>.claude/skills/md-gb/<=
/code> in that
repository instead. Claude Code loads it when you write HTML, Lit templates=
, or
CSS that use <code>md-gb-*</code> elements.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"about-ai-agents--install-it-from-this-site" tabindex=3D"-1">Insta=
ll it from this site</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-ai-agents--install-it-from-this-site"><s=
pan class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CInstall it from this site=E2=80=9D=
</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Without a checkout, the skill files are published at <code>/3.0/skill/</=
code>. The page tools
button (bottom end of every page) opens Download &amp; copy, which has Copy=
 agent
prompt: paste it into your agent and it
creates the skills folder, downloads <code>SKILL.md</code> and every <code>=
reference/*.md</code> file
listed in <code>/3.0/skill/index.json</code>, installs <code>@material/web<=
/code>, and checks the
result.</p>
<p>The same menu downloads the whole API as one <code>custom-elements.json<=
/code> (a
<a href=3D"https://github.com/webcomponents/custom-elements-manifest">Custo=
m Elements Manifest</a>
of every element), and <code>/3.0/llms.txt</code> indexes the docs as Markd=
own.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-ai-agents--keep-it-current" tabindex=3D"-1">Keep it current=
</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-ai-agents--keep-it-current"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CKeep it current=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-=
hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The skill is generated from the component sources and <code>scripts/m3/C=
HECKLIST.md</code>.
Do not edit it by hand. To regenerate it, run:</p>

<lit-island import=3D"/js/hydration-entrypoints/copy-code-button.js" on:int=
eraction=3D"focusin,pointerenter,touchstart">
  <div class=3D"gb-code"><pre class=3D"language-sh" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"=
region" aria-label=3D"Code 27"><code class=3D"language-sh"><span class=3D"t=
oken function">node</span> scripts/m3/gen-agent-skill.mjs</code></pre></div=
>
</lit-island>
<p>Run the same command with <code>--check</code> to fail when the output i=
s stale. After you
change a component, regenerate the skill and copy it again, because an inst=
alled
copy does not update itself.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-ai-agents--browser-agents-(webmcp)" tabindex=3D"-1">Browser=
 agents (WebMCP)</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-ai-agents--browser-agents-(webmcp)"><spa=
n class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CBrowser agents (WebMCP)=E2=80=9D</sp=
an> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>On every page of these docs, a browser that supports
<a href=3D"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/">WebMCP</a> lets it=
s agent search and
read the docs through five read-only tools. Nothing is registered in other
browsers. The tools use the same search as the Cmd+K dialog, and every page=
 is
also available as Markdown at its URL plus <code>.md</code>.</p>
<ul>
<li><code>search_docs</code> finds sections by keywords: <code>{query, limi=
t?}</code>.</li>
<li><code>get_page</code> returns a page or one section as Markdown: <code>=
{path, section?}</code>.</li>
<li><code>list_pages</code> lists the pages, optionally of one section: <co=
de>{section?}</code>.</li>
<li><code>get_component_api</code> returns the properties, slots, events, m=
ethods, CSS parts
and custom properties of an element: <code>{tag}</code>.</li>
<li><code>get_current_page</code> describes the page the user is on, with i=
ts outline.</li>
</ul>
<p>An agent calls them through the browser. This demo calls the same functi=
ons the
page registers (<code>window.gbDocsTools</code>) and shows the first three =
results of a
search.</p>
