<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"about-debugging" aria-labelledby=3D"ab=
out-debugging-title"><h1 id=3D"about-debugging-title">Debugging</h1><p clas=
s=3D"gb-lede">The shared plumbing of the components (motion waits, overflow=
 measure passes, and scroll steps) can record performance marks.</p><p clas=
s=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/about/d=
ebugging/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/about/debugging/</a></p><div class=
=3D"gb-content"><div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-debugging--performance-track" tabindex=3D"-1">Performance t=
rack</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-debugging--performance-track"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CPerformance track=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The shared plumbing of the components (motion waits, overflow measure pa=
sses,
and scroll steps) can record performance marks. They show up in the Chrome
DevTools Performance panel as a custom track named <code>md-gb</code>, in t=
he group
<code>Material</code>. The marks are off by default.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-debugging--turn-them-on" tabindex=3D"-1">Turn them on</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-debugging--turn-them-on"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CTurn them on=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The flag is read once, on first use, so set it before you interact with =
the
components. Use any one of these:</p>
<ul>
<li>Add <code>?md-gb-perf</code> to the page address and load it.</li>
<li>Set the flag in the console, then reload. Any value turns the marks on,=
 even
<code>0</code>. Remove the key to turn them off (the first sample below).</=
li>
<li>Set <code>globalThis.MD_GB_DEBUG_PERF =3D true</code> before any compon=
ent runs (the
second sample below).</li>
</ul>
