<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-shadcn--the-theme-bridge" tabindex=3D"-1">The theme bridge<=
/h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-shadcn--the-theme-bridge"><span class=3D=
"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CThe theme bridge=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>md-theme</code> adds <code>@import "@material/web/labs/gb/styles/m=
3.css"</code> to your global
CSS, then declares the <code>--md-sys-*</code> variables in <code>:root</co=
de> and in <code>.dark</code> from
your shadcn variables. The M3 styles are in a cascade layer and the bridge =
is
not, so the bridge wins regardless of the order of the imports. Change your
shadcn theme, or toggle <code>.dark</code>, and the elements follow. It als=
o sets
<code>color-scheme</code> for <code>:root</code> and <code>.dark</code>.</p=
>
<p>Containers stay with their <code>on-</code> colors: each pair maps to a =
pair that shadcn
already keeps readable together. The *-fixed roles, <code>scrim</code> and =
<code>shadow</code> keep
the M3 baseline.</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
8"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>M3 role</th>
<th>shadcn value</th>
<th>Why</th>
</tr>
</thead>
