<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"about-shadcn--limits" tabindex=3D"-1">Limits</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#about-shadcn--limits"><span class=3D"offscreen=
">Link to =E2=80=9CLimits=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</spa=
n></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tailwind classes style only the host.</strong> The elements use=
 shadow DOM, so
<code>className=3D"bg-red-500"</code> colors the <code>&lt;md-gb-button&gt;=
</code> box, not its inside.
Customize with the <code>--md-*</code> custom properties and <code>::part()=
</code> selectors
listed in each component's API reference. They work in a plain CSS file or =
in
Tailwind's arbitrary properties, such as <code>[--container-color:red]</cod=
e>.</li>
<li><strong>Client only.</strong> The wrappers start with <code>'use client=
'</code>, and the elements
cannot be imported in Node (they use CSS module scripts, <code>customElemen=
ts</code>
and <code>document</code>). In Next.js the server renders client components=
 too, so
import the file with
<code>next/dynamic(() =3D&gt; import('...'), {ssr: false})</code> or render=
 it after mount,
unless you set up <a href=3D"https://lit.dev/docs/ssr/overview/">Lit SSR</a=
>.</li>
<li><strong>Labs.</strong> The elements come from <code>@material/web/labs/=
gb/</code>. The registry
keeps <code>@material/web</code> as the dependency, and the path needs a ve=
rsion that
ships <code>labs/gb</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Typography, motion and icons</strong> are not bridged. Load the=
 Material
Symbols font as in the <a href=3D"#about-quick-start">quick start</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Local testing.</strong> When this site runs from the dev server=
 the registry
files point to <code>http://localhost:8000</code>. Set <code>MWC_REGISTRY_U=
RL</code> to build
them for another origin.</li>
</ul>
<p>The registry files are generated by <code>scripts/m3/gb-shadcn.mjs</code=
> from the element
sources, so the props and events match the API reference. For agents, the s=
ame
information is in <a href=3D"/3.0/llms.txt"><code>llms.txt</code></a> and
<a href=3D"/3.0/custom-elements.json"><code>custom-elements.json</code></a>=
.</p>
</div></section>
