<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"foundations-interaction-states" aria-l=
abelledby=3D"foundations-interaction-states-title"><h1 id=3D"foundations-in=
teraction-states-title">Interaction States</h1><p class=3D"gb-lede">Interac=
tive components show their state with a state layer: a translucent overlay =
of the component's content color, drawn between the container and the conte=
nt.</p><p class=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.d=
ev/3.0/foundations/interaction-states/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/founda=
tions/interaction-states/</a></p><div class=3D"gb-content"><p>Interactive c=
omponents show their state with a <strong>state layer</strong>: a transluce=
nt
overlay of the component's content color, drawn between the container and t=
he
content. Components handle this for you. You only need to know which state
shows which layer.</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
11"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>State</th>
<th>Layer opacity</th>
<th>When</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Hover</td>
<td>8%</td>
<td>A cursor rests over the element (hover-capable input)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Focus</td>
<td>10%</td>
<td>Keyboard or voice focus</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Pressed</td>
<td>10%</td>
<td>A tap or click is in progress</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dragged</td>
<td>16%</td>
<td>The element is being dragged</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Hover and focus combine. A focused, hovered element shows the focus laye=
r
too. Disabled components show no state layers: they cannot be focused,
dragged or pressed, and they do not inherit hover.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-interaction-states--hover-only-where-it-is-real" tabi=
ndex=3D"-1">Hover only where it is real</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-interaction-states--hover-only-whe=
re-it-is-real"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CHover only where =
it is real=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Hover applies only on devices that can hover, through <code>@media (hove=
r: hover)</code>.
A tap on a touch screen does not leave the hover layer on. Do not hide
essential content or controls behind hover, because touch users never see i=
t.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-interaction-states--pressed-ripple" tabindex=3D"-1">P=
ressed ripple</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-interaction-states--pressed-ripple=
"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CPressed ripple=E2=80=9D</span>=
 <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The pressed state plays a ripple, with this timing:</p>
<ul>
<li>The layer fades in over <strong>75ms</strong>.</li>
<li>The circle grows over <strong>225ms</strong> (fast-out, slow-in), while=
 its center moves
to the middle.</li>
<li>Once the press is released and the growth is done, the layer fades out =
over
<strong>150ms</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p>A quick tap still shows the ripple for at least 225ms, so a press always=
 reads
as a press.</p>
<p>Use the ripple as written. Do not add a second press effect on top of it=
.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
