<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"foundations-accessibility" aria-labell=
edby=3D"foundations-accessibility-title"><h1 id=3D"foundations-accessibilit=
y-title">Accessibility</h1><p class=3D"gb-lede">Every labs/gb component wor=
ks with a keyboard, a screen reader and reduced motion.</p><p class=3D"gb-a=
ll-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/foundations/acce=
ssibility/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/foundations/accessibility/</a></p>=
<div class=3D"gb-content"><p>The rules below are the ones the components fo=
llow and the tests check.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-accessibility--keyboard" tabindex=3D"-1">Keyboard</h2=
>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-accessibility--keyboard"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CKeyboard=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Composite components (button groups, chip sets, lists, menus, tabs, navi=
gation,
pickers) share one roving focus model in <code>labs/gb/components/shared/ro=
ving-focus.ts</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Arrow keys move between items along the orientation. Left and Right fol=
low
the reading direction, so they mirror in RTL.</li>
<li>Home and End go to the first and last item. Focus wraps at the ends unl=
ess
the component turns wrapping off.</li>
<li>Disabled items are skipped. Soft-disabled items stay focusable.</li>
<li>Only one item is in the tab order at a time (roving tabindex). Tab ente=
rs the
group on the item that was focused last, or the first one.</li>
<li>Keys pressed with Alt, Ctrl, Meta or Shift are left to the browser.</li=
>
</ul>
<p>Escape clears keyboard focus: it hides the focus indicator and starts th=
e focus
order over, so Tab after Escape reaches the first focusable element again. =
In a
text field, Escape removes the cursor and keeps the typed text. If a handle=
r
already used the Escape key, the component leaves it alone.</p>
<p>A dialog fires <code>cancel</code> on Escape, a scrim click or the full-=
screen close
button. Canceling keeps the dialog open if you call <code>preventDefault()<=
/code>:</p>
