<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-accessibility--focus-ring" tabindex=3D"-1">Focus ring=
</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-accessibility--focus-ring"><span c=
lass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CFocus ring=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-h=
idden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The focus ring is drawn with <code>outline</code>, using the <code>--foc=
us-ring-outline</code> and
<code>--focus-ring-offset</code> variables from <code>labs/gb/components/fo=
cus/focus-ring.scss</code>.
The thickness, color and offsets come from the state focus indicator tokens=
, so
a theme changes them in one place. Do not remove the outline with CSS unles=
s
you draw a replacement that passes the same tests.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-accessibility--screen-readers-and-aria" tabindex=3D"-=
1">Screen readers and ARIA</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-accessibility--screen-readers-and-=
aria"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CScreen readers and ARIA=E2=
=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Components use WAI-ARIA 1.3 roles, states and properties. The model of t=
he
draft and the checks that report misuse live in
<code>labs/gb/components/shared/central/aria_test.ts</code>. Axe-core runs =
against every
component in <code>labs/gb/components/shared/central/axe_test.ts</code>, so=
 a missing
label or an invalid attribute fails the suite.</p>
<p>Material Design 3 wins where it and WAI-ARIA 1.3 disagree. In every othe=
r case
the ARIA rules apply as written. When you add a component, follow the M3 pa=
ge
for its behavior first, then check the ARIA role and attributes it uses.</p=
>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-accessibility--reduced-motion" tabindex=3D"-1">Reduce=
d motion</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-accessibility--reduced-motion"><sp=
an class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CReduced motion=E2=80=9D</span> <spa=
n aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Motion respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code>. The motion =
helpers in
<code>labs/gb/components/shared/motion.ts</code> resolve to 0 ms under that=
 setting and
inside an ancestor with the <code>md-motion-reduced</code> class. The motio=
n tokens in
<code>labs/gb/styles/motion/</code> follow the same rule. Ripples skip the =
animated press
and show their end state, and the effect tokens (color, opacity, shape) do =
not
change.</p>
<p>Do not animate with hard-coded durations. Read the duration from the mot=
ion
helpers or the tokens, so reduced motion applies to your component too.</p>
</div></section>
