<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
12"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Class</th>
<th>Width (CSS px)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>compact</td>
<td>below 600</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>medium</td>
<td>600 to 839</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>expanded</td>
<td>840 to 1199</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>large</td>
<td>1200 to 1599</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>extra-large</td>
<td>1600 and up</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Height classes are compact (below 480), medium (480 to 899) and expanded=
 (900
and up). Most layouts scroll, so only use the height class when a component
needs it.</p>
<p>A component gets its class from <code>AdaptiveController</code> in
<code>labs/gb/components/shared/adaptive.ts</code>. The controller sets the
<code>window-size-class</code> attribute on the host, so CSS can match it. =
Options are
keyed by class and apply from that class up. Match the attribute in CSS and
use <code>atLeast('expanded')</code> in code. Do not read the window width =
directly.</p>
<p>In a Lit element, create the controller as a field and read <code>option=
s</code> in
<code>render()</code>. This sample uses a plain element as the host, so it =
runs without
Lit:</p>
