<p>Provide both a <code>md-gb-nav-bar</code> and a <code>md-gb-nav-rail</co=
de> with the same
destinations, and keep their selection in sync. The scaffold shows only one=
 of
them.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-adaptive-layout--panes" tabindex=3D"-1">Panes</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-adaptive-layout--panes"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CPanes=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D=
"true">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>md-gb-pane-scaffold</code> shows one, two or three panes. The defa=
ult slot is the
primary (flexible) pane, <code>secondary</code> is the list of a list-detai=
l layout, and
<code>tertiary</code> is an optional third pane, such as a standard side sh=
eet.
<code>placeholder</code> is shown in the primary pane of a two-pane layout =
with nothing
selected.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-adaptive-layout--safe-areas" tabindex=3D"-1">Safe are=
as</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-adaptive-layout--safe-areas"><span=
 class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CSafe areas=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The scaffold keeps its bars away from the device safe areas. It reads
<code>--md-gb-scaffold-safe-top</code>, <code>-right</code>, <code>-bottom<=
/code> and <code>-left</code>, which default to
<code>env(safe-area-inset-*)</code>. Keep primary content out of those edge=
s. To change
the insets, set the custom properties on the scaffold.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-adaptive-layout--full-screen-dialogs" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Full-screen dialogs</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-adaptive-layout--full-screen-dialo=
gs"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CFull-screen dialogs=E2=80=9D=
</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>A full-screen dialog is for compact windows only. Set <code>full-screen<=
/code> on
<code>md-gb-dialog</code>: at compact it fills the window, and at medium an=
d larger it
falls back to a basic dialog with the same slots. Set <code>always-full-scr=
een</code>
to keep the full-screen variant at every size, if the task needs it.</p>
</div></section>
<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"foundations-density" aria-labelledby=
=3D"foundations-density-title"><h1 id=3D"foundations-density-title">Density=
</h1><p class=3D"gb-lede">Density lets people see more information in data-=
heavy views by making components more compact.</p><p class=3D"gb-all-source=
">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/foundations/density/">htt=
ps://material-web.dev/3.0/foundations/density/</a></p><div class=3D"gb-cont=
ent"><p>Density lets people see more information in data-heavy views by mak=
ing
components more compact. A component's density is a number from <code>0</co=
de> (the
default) to <code>-3</code> (the densest). Each step down makes the compone=
nt smaller.
Values are rounded and clamped to that range.</p>
<p>Use the <code>density</code> attribute.</p>
