<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-density--which-components-support-it" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Which components support it</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-density--which-components-support-=
it"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhich components support it=
=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>density</code> is available on these components:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>md-gb-button-group</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-checkbox</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-chip</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-icon-button</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-list</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-menu</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-radio</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-segmented-button</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-switch</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-tabs</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-text-field</code></li>
<li><code>md-gb-time-picker</code></li>
</ul>
<p>Each step shrinks the component's visual size, not its touch target. A
checkbox, for example, loses 4px from its layout box (48px at density 0) an=
d
its state layer (40px at density 0) per step. Its touch target stays 48px.<=
/p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-density--touch-targets-stay-48dp" tabindex=3D"-1">Tou=
ch targets stay 48dp</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-density--touch-targets-stay-48dp">=
<span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CTouch targets stay 48dp=E2=80=9D=
</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Every component keeps a touch target of at least 48 by 48 CSS pixels, ev=
en at
the densest setting. The visual element can be smaller, but the area that
responds to a tap cannot. Do not override this with your own sizing.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-density--rules-of-thumb" tabindex=3D"-1">Rules of thu=
mb</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-density--rules-of-thumb"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CRules of thumb=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Density is a choice, not a default.</strong> Leave components a=
t <code>0</code> unless the
view is data-heavy, and let people opt into a denser layout where you offer
a control for it.</li>
<li><strong>Do not change density automatically.</strong> It should not swi=
tch when the
window resizes or the device rotates, unless the person changed it.</li>
<li><strong>Consider the device.</strong> A person may want a dense desktop=
 layout but not a
dense phone layout.</li>
<li><strong>Layout density comes first.</strong> Spacing changes can add in=
formation without
shrinking components. Use component density when you also need the
controls themselves to be smaller.</li>
<li><strong>Keep the controls accessible.</strong> If you offer a density s=
etting, the
setting itself must be easy to find and use.</li>
</ul>
</div></section>
<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"foundations-layout" aria-labelledby=3D=
"foundations-layout-title"><h1 id=3D"foundations-layout-title">Layout</h1><=
p class=3D"gb-lede">Layout adapts an app to the window with window size cla=
sses, a column grid, margins and panes.</p><p class=3D"gb-all-source">Onlin=
e: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/foundations/layout/">https://mat=
erial-web.dev/3.0/foundations/layout/</a></p><div class=3D"gb-content"><p>L=
ayout adapts an app to the window. The window size class (see
<a href=3D"#foundations-adaptive-layout--window-size-classes">Adaptive layo=
ut</a>)
sets the layout tokens
on <code>:root</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>--md-sys-layout-columns</code>: 4 at compact, 8 at medium and exp=
anded, 12 from
large up.</li>
<li><code>--md-sys-layout-margin</code>: 16px at compact, 24px above.</li>
<li><code>--md-sys-layout-spacer</code>: the gutter between columns, 16px a=
t compact,
24px above.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-layout--window-size-classes-and-grid" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Window size classes and grid</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-layout--window-size-classes-and-gr=
id"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWindow size classes and grid=
=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>.md-layout-grid</code> lays its children out on the column grid, w=
ith the margin as
inline padding and the spacer as the gap.</p>
