<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-scaffold--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage gui=
delines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-scaffold--usage-guidelines"><span =
class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span=
 aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Structure the app in bars, rails and panes.</strong> Bars frame=
 the page, rails run along its edges, and panes hold the content.</li>
<li><strong>Provide both navigation components.</strong> Give the scaffold =
a navigation bar and a navigation rail with the same destinations. It shows=
 the bar in compact windows and the rail from medium windows up, and you ke=
ep their selection in sync.</li>
<li><strong>Pick the pane layout by content.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#found=
ations-scaffold--list-detail">list-detail</a> for a collection and its deta=
ils, <a href=3D"#foundations-scaffold--supporting-pane">supporting pane</a>=
 for a focus area with related content, and <a href=3D"#foundations-scaffol=
d--feed">feed</a> for a grid of items.</li>
<li><strong>Use one to three panes.</strong> The number of visible panes fo=
llows the window size.</li>
</ul>
<p>This component is new in <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/blog/building=
-with-m3-expressive">M3 Expressive</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"foundations-scaffold--anatomy" tabindex=3D"-1">Anatomy</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-scaffold--anatomy"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAnatomy=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue">#</span></a></div>
<p><code>md-gb-app-scaffold</code> places bars and rails around its content=
. <code>md-gb-pane-scaffold</code> goes in the content and arranges the pan=
es.</p>
