<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"foundations-scaffold--floating-and-docked-panes" tabindex=3D"-1">=
Floating and docked panes</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#foundations-scaffold--floating-and-docked-pane=
s"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CFloating and docked panes=E2=
=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>When there is no room for a supporting pane beside the content, set <cod=
e>levitate</code> to <code>floating</code> or <code>docked</code> to lift t=
he <code>secondary</code> pane above it instead of stacking it below. A doc=
ked pane sits at the bottom edge on compact windows, like a bottom sheet. O=
pen it with <code>openLevitated()</code> and close it with <code>closeLevit=
ated()</code>. Add <code>levitate-modal</code> for a scrim, and <code>levit=
ate-label</code> to name the pane.</p>
<figure class=3D"gb-demo" aria-label=3D"A button that opens a floating supp=
orting pane of comments" id=3D"gbd-1ded60">
