<p>The seed (or the core primary) is the source, other core colors become
<code>palettes</code>, extended colors become harmonized or exact <code>cus=
tomColors</code>, and a
<code>variant</code> or <code>contrast</code> field in the file is used if =
present. The generated
schemes and palettes in the export are ignored, so the roles match the rest=
 of
labs/gb. A second argument overrides any option.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-color--dynamic-color" tabindex=3D"-1">Dynamic color</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-color--dynamic-color"><span class=3D"of=
fscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CDynamic color=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>A dynamic scheme is generated from a source. The spec distinguishes
<strong>user-generated</strong> color (a wallpaper or a person's pick, usua=
lly with the
<code>tonal-spot</code> variant), <strong>content-based</strong> color (tak=
en from an image or content
on screen, with the <code>content</code> variant), and <strong>multiple sou=
rces</strong> (several
schemes on one screen, each scoped to a region).</p>
