<p>Harmonize colors that carry meaning but should still sit in the theme, s=
uch
as success and warning. Do not harmonize brand colors that must stay exact.=
</p>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-color--custom-color-roles" tabindex=3D"-1">Custom color ro=
les</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-color--custom-color-roles"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CCustom color roles=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>A custom role is one color picked from a palette at a reference tone, fo=
r light
and dark, so it follows the source color and the contrast level like the
built-in roles. It makes <code>--md-sys-color-&lt;name&gt;</code> only; pic=
k a tone that
meets contrast against the role it sits on (3:1 for graphics) and check the
pair yourself.</p>
