<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"styles-typography" aria-labelledby=3D"=
styles-typography-title"><h1 id=3D"styles-typography-title">Typography</h1>=
<p class=3D"gb-lede">Typography helps make writing legible and beautiful.</=
p><p class=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.=
0/styles/typography/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/typography/</a></=
p><div class=3D"gb-content"><blockquote>
<p>Tip: "typeface" and "typescale" can be confusing. "face" refers to
<code>font-family</code> and <code>font-weight</code>.</p>
<p>"scale" refers to a group of <code>font-family</code>, <code>font-size</=
code>, <code>line-height</code>, and
<code>font-weight</code> tokens.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-typography--typeface" tabindex=3D"-1">Typeface</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-typography--typeface"><span class=3D"of=
fscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CTypeface=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"tru=
e">#</span></a></div>
<p>A <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/styles/typography/fonts">typeface</a=
> is a
<code>font-family</code>. In Material there are plain and brand typefaces.<=
/p>
<p>Each typeface has normal, medium, and bold styles (defaults to <code>400=
</code>, <code>500</code>, and
<code>700</code>). All three weight styles need to be included for a font.<=
/p>
<blockquote>
<p>Important: the default typeface is Roboto Flex, then Roboto. If you do n=
ot
change it, load one of them. For example, from
<a href=3D"https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Roboto+Flex">fonts.google.com<=
/a>.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-typography--tokens" tabindex=3D"-1">Tokens</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-typography--tokens"><span class=3D"offs=
creen">Link to =E2=80=9CTokens=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#=
</span></a></div>
<p>Typefaces can be set using
<a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/--*">CSS custom=
 properties</a>.
Tokens follow the naming convention <code>--md-ref-typeface-&lt;token&gt;</=
code>.</p>
