<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"styles-shape" aria-labelledby=3D"style=
s-shape-title"><h1 id=3D"styles-shape-title">Shape</h1><p class=3D"gb-lede"=
>Shape can direct attention, communicate state, and express brand.</p><p cl=
ass=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/style=
s/shape/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/shape/</a></p><div class=3D"g=
b-content"><p>M3 Expressive uses a
<a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/styles/shape/corner-radius-scale">corner =
radius scale</a>
from straight to fully round, with larger steps, "increased" values, and sh=
ape
morphing between states.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-shape--tokens" tabindex=3D"-1">Tokens</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-shape--tokens"><span class=3D"offscreen=
">Link to =E2=80=9CTokens=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</spa=
n></a></div>
<p>Tokens follow the naming convention <code>--md-sys-shape-corner-&lt;step=
&gt;</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
28"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Shape</th>
<th>Token</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Corner</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-none</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-xs</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-sm</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-md</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-lg</code>, <code>-lg-increased</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-xl</code>, <code>-xl-increased</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-xxl</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>&nbsp;</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-full</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Steps also come in asymmetric variants (<code>-xs-top</code>, <code>-lg-=
top</code>, <code>-lg-start</code>,
<code>-lg-end</code>, <code>-xl-top</code>) and as single values
(<code>--md-sys-shape-corner-value-&lt;step&gt;</code>). Each step also has=
 one token per corner,
such as <code>--md-sys-shape-corner-md-start-end</code>, which defaults to =
the step's
all-corner token; override one to shape a single corner.</p>
<p><code>--md-sys-shape-corner-full</code> is <code>50cqmin</code> (half th=
e shorter side of the nearest
size container), so it rounds fully only inside a container. Components tha=
t
animate through "full" set it to half their own height.</p>
