<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-elevation--what-to-watch-out-for" tabindex=3D"-1">What to =
watch out for</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-elevation--what-to-watch-out-for"><span=
 class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhat to watch out for=E2=80=9D</span>=
 <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Do not hard-code shadow values. Use the level tokens so a change to the
scale reaches every surface.</li>
<li>Avoid changing the default elevation of a component. When an interactio=
n such
as hover changes it, make the change the same for every similar component.<=
/li>
<li>Give floating elements enough contrast with the surface beneath them, e=
ither
through the shadow or through a tone difference.</li>
</ul>
</div></section>
<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"styles-icons" aria-labelledby=3D"style=
s-icons-title"><h1 id=3D"styles-icons-title">Icons</h1><p class=3D"gb-lede"=
>md-gb-icon shows a Material Symbols icon.</p><p class=3D"gb-all-source">On=
line: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/icons/">https://materi=
al-web.dev/3.0/styles/icons/</a></p><div class=3D"gb-content"><p><code>md-g=
b-icon</code> shows a Material Symbols icon. Its content is the ligature na=
me
of the symbol, such as <code>home</code>. Find names and previews at
<a href=3D"https://fonts.google.com/icons">fonts.google.com/icons</a>. Symb=
ols come in three
styles: outlined, rounded and sharp.</p>
<p>The element is a thin wrapper over the font. It reads its size, color an=
d font
variation settings from custom properties.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--loading-the-font" tabindex=3D"-1">Loading the font<=
/h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--loading-the-font"><span class=3D=
"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CLoading the font=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The element's default font family is <code>Material Symbols</code>. The =
Google Fonts
family for the outlined style is <code>Material Symbols Outlined</code>, so=
