<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--size-and-color" tabindex=3D"-1">Size and color</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--size-and-color"><span class=3D"o=
ffscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CSize and color=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><code>--md-icon-size</code> sets the size. The default is <code>24px</c=
ode>. Symbols support 20dp,
24dp, 40dp and 48dp; use 20dp for dense layouts and 40dp or 48dp for displa=
y
use.</li>
<li><code>--md-icon-color</code> sets the color. The default is <code>curre=
ntColor</code>.</li>
<li>The optical size follows the icon size automatically, so a larger icon =
gets a
matching optical size. Set <code>--md-icon-opsz</code> only to override it.=
</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--variable-font-axes" tabindex=3D"-1">Variable font a=
xes</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--variable-font-axes"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CVariable font axes=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Each style has four axes. The element exposes them as custom properties:=
</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
30"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Axis</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Range</th>
<th>Notes</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-icon-wght</code></td>
<td>Weight</td>
<td><code>400</code></td>
<td>100 to 700</td>
<td>400 is the 2dp stroke for standard icons. Use at least 200 at 24dp.</td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-icon-fill</code></td>
<td>Fill</td>
<td><code>0</code></td>
<td>0 to 1</td>
<td>1 is filled, 0 is outlined. The change animates.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-icon-grad</code></td>
<td>Grade</td>
<td><code>0</code></td>
<td>Negative to positive</td>
<td>Gb sets <code>-25</code> when the color scheme is dark, where icons are=
 light on dark. Positive values add emphasis.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-icon-opsz</code></td>
<td>Optical size</td>
<td>follows size</td>
<td>20 to 48dp</td>
<td>Not set by default.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Fill is the usual way to show a selected state. Use the outlined symbol =
when
the item is unselected and the filled one when it is selected.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--baseline-next-to-text" tabindex=3D"-1">Baseline nex=
t to text</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--baseline-next-to-text"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CBaseline next to text=E2=80=9D</span> <sp=
an aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Symbols next to text need a baseline shift to line up. The element alrea=
dy
applies <code>vertical-align: -0.115em</code> (of its own size), which lowe=
rs the icon so
it lines up with the text beside it: about 2.8px at 24dp. Keep that <code>v=
ertical-align</code> if you override the
style, or the icon will look too high.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--targets" tabindex=3D"-1">Targets</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--targets"><span class=3D"offscree=
n">Link to =E2=80=9CTargets=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</s=
pan></a></div>
<p>A 24dp icon needs a 48dp target by default. A 20dp icon can use a 40dp t=
arget
when a mouse and keyboard are the main input. <code>md-gb-icon-button</code=
> keeps a 48dp
minimum target (<code>--target-size</code>) even when the icon inside is sm=
aller, so use it
rather than a bare icon in a clickable element.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--accessibility"><span class=3D"of=
fscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>An icon is decorative unless it has a label. <code>md-gb-icon</code> se=
ts
<code>aria-hidden=3D"true"</code> by default, so screen readers skip it. Th=
at is correct
when the text beside the icon already says what it means.</li>
<li>For an icon-only control, put the accessible name on the control with
<code>aria-label</code>, and leave the icon hidden. Only set <code>aria-hid=
den=3D"false"</code> on an
icon that must be announced on its own.</li>
<li>Add a text label when the symbol is abstract, complex, or carries a key
action. A symbol shown below 20dp should have one too.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--examples" tabindex=3D"-1">Examples</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--examples"><span class=3D"offscre=
en">Link to =E2=80=9CExamples=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#<=
/span></a></div>
<p>Change an axis or the size with the custom properties.</p>
