<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-icons--what-to-watch-out-for" tabindex=3D"-1">What to watc=
h out for</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-icons--what-to-watch-out-for"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhat to watch out for=E2=80=9D</span> <sp=
an aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>An icon with no font loaded shows the ligature text, such as <code>favo=
rite</code>, not
a symbol. Load the font before the page relies on it.</li>
<li>Do not mix styles in one icon set. Pick outlined, rounded or sharp for =
the
whole product.</li>
<li>Do not use the lightest weight for standard 24dp icons.</li>
<li>Keep the icon's content inside the 20dp live area of the 24dp grid. It =
can
reach into the 2dp padding for extra weight, but never past the 24dp edge.<=
/li>
</ul>
</div></section>
