<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"styles-motion" aria-labelledby=3D"styl=
es-motion-title"><h1 id=3D"styles-motion-title">Motion</h1><p class=3D"gb-l=
ede">Motion makes a UI expressive and easy to follow: springs for physics, =
easing and duration tokens, and transition patterns.</p><p class=3D"gb-all-=
source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/motion/">htt=
ps://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/motion/</a></p><div class=3D"gb-content"><=
div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-motion--overview" tabindex=3D"-1">Overview</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--overview"><span class=3D"offscr=
een">Link to =E2=80=9COverview=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#=
</span></a></div>
<p>Material 3 Expressive uses a physics-based motion system. Springs drive
spatial motion (position, size, rotation, corner shape) and effects springs
drive properties that must not overshoot, like color and opacity. One sprin=
g
can serve transitions, button effects and gestures, which keeps the product
feeling consistent. Each spring is exposed as a CSS <code>linear()</code> e=
asing with a
matching duration, so a transition can use it directly.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--motion-schemes" tabindex=3D"-1">Motion schemes</h3=
>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--motion-schemes"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CMotion schemes=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Expressive</strong> is the default. Use it for most situations,=
 especially hero
moments and key interactions. Spatial springs overshoot and bounce into
place.</li>
<li><strong>Standard</strong> moves with minimal bounce and suits utilitari=
an products. Apply
it to a subtree with the <code>md-motion-standard</code> class.</li>
</ul>
<p>The spec's three levels of customization map to CSS like this:</p>
<ol>
<li>Use a default scheme: do nothing (Expressive), or add <code>md-motion-s=
tandard</code>.</li>
<li>Create a custom scheme: override the spring custom properties in your o=
wn
<code>:root</code> rule.</li>
<li>Swap the scheme for one element: put <code>md-motion-standard</code> on=
 that element.</li>
</ol>
<figure class=3D"gb-demo" aria-label=3D"A button in a subtree that uses the=
 standard motion scheme" id=3D"gbd-d8851c" data-short=3D"">
