<p>Under reduced motion the spring jumps to its target and rests at once.
<code>DragSettleController</code> (the drag-and-settle behavior behind swip=
e to reveal,
drawers, sheets and pane handles) does this for you when you pass <code>onF=
rame</code>: the settle starts at the release
position with the release velocity, and the surface follows the frames with=
 no
CSS transition on the moved property. Without <code>onFrame</code> it keeps=
 the CSS
transition of the spring token.</p>
