>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--shape-morphing"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CShape morphing=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Buttons and icon buttons (<code>md-gb-button</code>, <code>md-gb-icon-bu=
tton</code>) morph their
shape when pressed and when selected. That is spatial motion, so reduced
motion turns it off and keeps the color change.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--component-authors" tabindex=3D"-1">Component autho=
rs</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--component-authors"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CComponent authors=E2=80=9D</span> <span ari=
a-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Components that script their motion use the helpers in
<code>labs/gb/components/shared/motion.ts</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>springDuration(element, speed, kind)</code> returns the duration =
of a spring in
milliseconds, already 0 for spatial springs when motion is reduced.</li>
<li><code>isReducedMotion(element)</code> and <code>onReducedMotionChange(.=
..)</code> follow the
setting, including inside <code>.md-motion-reduced</code>.</li>
<li><code>waitForMotion(...)</code> resolves when the animations end or whe=
n its timeout
runs out, so waiting never hangs. <code>waitForDuration(ms, signal)</code> =
is the
plain timed wait.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--not-covered" tabindex=3D"-1">Not covered</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--not-covered"><span class=3D"off=
screen">Link to =E2=80=9CNot covered=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"t=
rue">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>The spec's Compose APIs (<code>MotionScheme</code> objects, a <code>Com=
positionLocal</code> per
element) have no web equivalent. The CSS steps above replace them.</li>
<li>Springs are pre-sampled into <code>linear()</code> easings for transiti=
ons. A
transition cannot take a starting velocity, so gestures use the solver
described in <a href=3D"#styles-motion--gestures">Gestures</a> instead.</li=
>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-motion--easing-and-duration" tabindex=3D"-1">Easing and du=
ration</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--easing-and-duration"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CEasing and duration=E2=80=9D</span> <span =
aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>M3 Expressive moves components to springs, but transitions still use the
easing and duration system, and so can products that have not migrated yet.
The spec offers a starting pair for each case:</p>
