<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--top-level" tabindex=3D"-1">Top level</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--top-level"><span class=3D"offsc=
reen">Link to =E2=80=9CTop level=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true"=
>#</span></a></div>
<p>For switching between top-level destinations (navigation bar, rail or dr=
awer).
The old screen quickly fades out, then the new one fades in, so they never
overlap. These destinations are not related spatially, so there is no
directional slide; the new screen only scales up slightly as it fades in.</=
p>
