<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--enter-and-exit" tabindex=3D"-1">Enter and exit</h3=
>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--enter-and-exit"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CEnter and exit=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>For introducing or removing a component. <code>enter(element, options)</=
code> shows it
(<code>hidden =3D false</code>) and <code>exit(element, options)</code> ani=
mates it away, then you hide
or remove it. Both resolve when the animation ends.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Within screen bounds</strong> (menus, dialogs, snackbars, toolt=
ips, FABs). The
default <code>style: 'expand'</code> is the Android style: the component ex=
pands away
from the nearest screen edge, without scale. <code>style: 'scale'</code> is=
 the iOS
style (scale in, fade out). Pick the edge with <code>origin</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Beyond screen bounds</strong> (drawers, sheets, banners, naviga=
tion). <code>style: 'slide'</code> slides the component on and off from its=
 edge. Set <code>temporary: true</code>
for something that comes back, like a drawer, so it exits with the plain
Emphasized curve instead of the accelerate one.</li>
</ul>
