<p>Match the origin to where the component lives: a notification from the t=
op, a
drawer from the start edge, a bottom sheet and the keyboard from the bottom=
.
In templates, <code>enterExitClasses(state, options)</code> returns a <code=
>classMap()</code> object
(<code>md-transition-enter</code>, <code>md-transition-from-top</code> and =
so on), and
<code>clearEnterExit(element)</code> removes the classes.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h4">
<h4 id=3D"styles-motion--hide-and-reveal-while-scrolling" tabindex=3D"-1">H=
ide and reveal while scrolling</h4>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--hide-and-reveal-while-scrolling=
"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CHide and reveal while scrollin=
g=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>A component can also leave and return based on a scroll gesture, to give=
 more
room for browsing: a top app bar or a navigation bar that slides off the sc=
reen
edge while the user scrolls down and back on when they scroll up.
<code>scrollEnterExit(element, options)</code> does this with the slide ent=
er and exit
motion and returns a handle with <code>hidden</code>, <code>show()</code>, =
<code>hide()</code> and <code>destroy()</code>.</p>
