<p><code>axis: 'block'</code> grows the element along the block axis instea=
d of the inline
axis. With reduced motion the size changes at once and only a fade plays.
<code>md-gb-side-sheet</code> already does this itself: a standard (not mod=
al) sheet takes
its width as <code>open</code> is set, so the content beside it shrinks wit=
h its spring
motion. Use <code>coplanar()</code> for your own panels.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--skeleton-loaders" tabindex=3D"-1">Skeleton loaders=
</h3>
