<p><code>shape</code> is <code>rect</code>, <code>text</code> or <code>circ=
le</code>. While loading the element sets
<code>aria-busy=3D"true"</code> and makes its content inert. For markup wit=
hout the element,
use the classes <code>md-skeleton</code>, <code>md-skeleton-text</code> and=
 <code>md-skeleton-circle</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h3">
<h3 id=3D"styles-motion--accessibility-and-good-practice" tabindex=3D"-1">A=
ccessibility and good practice</h3>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--accessibility-and-good-practice=
"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility and good practic=
e=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The spec asks transitions to follow accessibility settings, stay consist=
ent,
keep layouts stable, avoid jump cuts, use one spatial model and direction, =
fade
cleanly and stay simple.</p>
<ul>
<li>Every helper follows <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> and replaces s=
liding and
scaling with a quick fade. Pass <code>reducedMotion: true</code> to force i=
t, as an app
setting would.</li>
<li>Fade through never overlaps the old and new content. The content fade o=
f a
container transform is timed to the fastest part of the motion.</li>
<li>Use one pattern per kind of navigation, and keep forward and backward
mirrored.</li>
<li>Dialogs and similar components that appear in place use the short fade
(<code>--md-transition-enter-fade-duration</code>).</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-motion--watch-out-for" tabindex=3D"-1">Watch out for</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion--watch-out-for"><span class=3D"o=
ffscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWatch out for=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Keep most of a product on one scheme. Switch schemes only for a few key
moments, and do it on purpose.</li>
<li>Do not use motion to carry meaning on its own. Reduced motion removes i=
t,
so pair it with a change people can see without motion.</li>
</ul>
</div></section>
<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"styles-motion-transitions" aria-labell=
edby=3D"styles-motion-transitions-title"><h1 id=3D"styles-motion-transition=
s-title">Transitions</h1><p class=3D"gb-lede">Transition patterns connect e=
lements and views, and skeleton loaders hold space while content loads.</p>=
<p class=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/=
styles/motion-transitions/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/motion-tran=
sitions/</a></p><div class=3D"gb-content"><p>The six transition patterns (c=
ontainer transform, forward and backward,
lateral, top level, enter and exit, and skeleton loaders) are helper functi=
ons
and classes. See <a href=3D"#styles-motion--transitions">Motion</a> for the=
 helpers.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-motion-transitions--skeleton-loaders" tabindex=3D"-1">Skel=
eton loaders</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-motion-transitions--skeleton-loaders"><=
span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CSkeleton loaders=E2=80=9D</span> =
<span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>A skeleton hints at where content will appear and holds its space while =
it
loads. Set <code>loading</code> and clear it when the content is ready.</p>
