<section class=3D"gb-all-page" id=3D"styles-spacing" aria-labelledby=3D"sty=
les-spacing-title"><h1 id=3D"styles-spacing-title">Spacing</h1><p class=3D"=
gb-lede">Spacing is the distance around and between elements.</p><p class=
=3D"gb-all-source">Online: <a href=3D"https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/s=
pacing/">https://material-web.dev/3.0/styles/spacing/</a></p><div class=3D"=
gb-content"><p>Spacing is the distance around and between elements. It shap=
es components
(the space between an icon and its label) and layouts (the margin between t=
he
content and the window edge). Spacing follows an 8dp scale, and tokens keep=
 that
scale in one place.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-spacing--parts-of-spacing" tabindex=3D"-1">Parts of spacin=
g</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-spacing--parts-of-spacing"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CParts of spacing=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>There are three kinds:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Padding</strong> is the space inside an element, between its ed=
ge and its
content.</li>
<li><strong>Gaps</strong> are the spaces between elements in a row, column =
or grid.</li>
<li><strong>Margins</strong> are the space outside an element, between it a=
nd its parent or
the screen edge.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each one can be vertical, horizontal, or on one edge: top, bottom, leadi=
ng or
trailing. Leading and trailing swap sides in right-to-left languages, so wr=
ite
them as logical properties (<code>padding-inline</code>, <code>margin-inlin=
e-start</code>).</p>
<p>Define padding and gaps on the parent container first. Margins on child
elements are harder to keep uniform, so use them only for space beyond the
parent's padding, or in a layout.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-spacing--the-scale" tabindex=3D"-1">The scale</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-spacing--the-scale"><span class=3D"offs=
creen">Link to =E2=80=9CThe scale=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true=
">#</span></a></div>
<p>The unit is <code>--md-sys-space-unit</code>, 8px. Each token is a multi=
ple of it. The
token name is the value times 100, so <code>space200</code> is 2 units (16p=
x). The
in-between values (2, 4, 6 and 10px) are nested units for small gaps, such =
as
an icon and its label.</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
33"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Token</th>
<th>Value</th>
<th>Token</th>
<th>Value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-0</code></td>
<td>0px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-400</code></td>
<td>32px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-25</code></td>
<td>2px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-450</code></td>
<td>36px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-50</code></td>
<td>4px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-500</code></td>
<td>40px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-75</code></td>
<td>6px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-600</code></td>
<td>48px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-100</code></td>
<td>8px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-700</code></td>
<td>56px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-125</code></td>
<td>10px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-800</code></td>
<td>64px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-150</code></td>
<td>12px</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-900</code></td>
<td>72px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-175</code></td>
<td>14px</td>
<td></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-200</code></td>
<td>16px</td>
<td></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-250</code></td>
<td>20px</td>
<td></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>--md-sys-space-300</code></td>
<td>24px</td>
<td></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>The tokens are defined in <code>labs/gb/styles/space/md-space-tokens.scs=
s</code>. They
are fixed pixel values, so they do not grow with the text size.</p>
<p>A product can add a token that follows the same pattern. For example,
<code>--md-sys-space-225: calc(var(--md-sys-space-unit) * 2.25)</code> give=
s 18px.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-spacing--adaptive-spacing" tabindex=3D"-1">Adaptive spacin=
g</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-spacing--adaptive-spacing"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAdaptive spacing=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Some spacing should change with the window. Three adaptive tokens do thi=
s:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>--md-sys-space-adaptive-inline</code>: horizontal padding</li>
<li><code>--md-sys-space-adaptive-block</code>: vertical padding</li>
<li><code>--md-sys-space-adaptive-gap</code>: gap between elements</li>
</ul>
<p>Each one points at a scale token that depends on the window size class. =
The
classes are the ones in <a href=3D"#foundations-adaptive-layout">Adaptive l=
ayout</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
34"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Class</th>
<th>Inline</th>
<th>Block</th>
<th>Gap</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>compact</td>
<td>16px</td>
<td>16px</td>
<td>8px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>medium</td>
<td>24px</td>
<td>24px</td>
<td>16px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>expanded</td>
<td>24px</td>
<td>32px</td>
<td>16px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>large</td>
<td>32px</td>
<td>32px</td>
<td>24px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>extra-large</td>
<td>32px</td>
<td>40px</td>
<td>24px</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Direct children of a <code>.md-window</code> element follow that element=
's width, so a
layout can adapt to its pane rather than the screen. Other elements follow =
the
viewport. The spacing unit does not change with the window.</p>
