<blockquote>
<p>The adaptive tokens are defined, but no labs/gb component reads them yet=
:
component spacing is the same at every window size today. Use them in your
own layouts, or remap a component's own spacing property to one (see below)=
.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-spacing--how-components-use-spacing" tabindex=3D"-1">How c=
omponents use spacing</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-spacing--how-components-use-spacing"><s=
pan class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CHow components use spacing=E2=80=
=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>Components map their padding, margins and gaps to scale tokens in their =
own
custom properties (<code>--leading-space</code>, <code>--icon-label-space</=
code> and so on), so a
product can change one mapping and every use follows. For example,
<code>md-gb-button { --leading-space: var(--md-sys-space-adaptive-inline); =
}</code> makes a
button's leading padding follow the window class.</p>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
35"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Component</th>
<th>Scale tokens it reads</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Button, icon button, FAB, split button, segmented button</td>
<td><code>space50</code> to <code>space200</code> for leading and trailing =
space and the icon-label gap</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Search bar</td>
<td><code>space0</code> to <code>space300</code>: leading space <code>space=
200</code>, icon and input gap <code>space50</code>, glyph margin <code>spa=
ce300</code> (24px), or <code>space150</code> (12px) when focused. Styles a=
re in <code>labs/gb/components/search/</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>App bar</td>
<td><code>space0</code> to <code>space300</code> for icon, leading and trai=
ling space, the title inset and bottom space, and the actions' inline margi=
n</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Toolbar, navigation drawer</td>
<td><code>space50</code> to <code>space200</code> for container padding and=
 item spacing</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Chip, text field, tooltip, menu, divider, badge, tabs</td>
<td><code>space25</code> to <code>space200</code> for padding, label gaps a=
nd insets</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Date picker, time picker, carousel</td>
<td><code>space50</code> to <code>space900</code> for header, actions and c=
ontent padding</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>App scaffold</td>
<td><code>space200</code> for the FAB's distance from the edge and the gap =
above the bottom bar</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Pane scaffold</td>
<td><code>--md-sys-layout-margin</code> and <code>--md-sys-layout-spacer</c=
ode> (the layout tokens), not the scale</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Every value is the same as before, so nothing changes visually. A few va=
lues
are still plain pixels: some generated button, list, FAB, button group and
navigation rail values, the dialog and sheet paddings, and the few values a
component reads in code (a carousel's leading padding, a tooltip's viewport
margin, a tab indicator's inset).</p>
<p>Density changes components, not the spacing scale. Each density step rem=
oves
height from the component, and the component's touch target stays 48dp. See
<a href=3D"#foundations-density">Density</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-spacing--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-spacing--accessibility"><span class=3D"=
offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>The spec's accessibility guidance is one point: when text is scaled up t=
o
200%, keep the same spacing. Spacing tokens are fixed in pixels, so the spa=
cing
stays the same while the text grows. For touch targets and focus, see
<a href=3D"#foundations-accessibility">Accessibility</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"styles-spacing--what-to-watch-out-for" tabindex=3D"-1">What to wa=
tch out for</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#styles-spacing--what-to-watch-out-for"><span c=
lass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CWhat to watch out for=E2=80=9D</span> <=
span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Use the scale tokens, not hardcoded pixel values. A raw <code>16px</cod=
e> will not
follow a remapped token.</li>
<li>Set spacing on the parent, not the children, unless you need space beyo=
nd
the parent's padding.</li>
<li>Use logical properties (<code>padding-inline</code>, <code>gap</code>) =
so right-to-left layouts
flip correctly.</li>
<li>Do not adapt spacing to density yourself. Set the <code>density</code> =
attribute on the
component and let it apply its own steps.</li>
<li>Keep the spacing the same at 200% text. Do not replace a token with a v=
alue
that grows with the text.</li>
</ul>
</div></section>
