<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-button-group--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage =
guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-button-group--usage-guidelines"><sp=
an class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <s=
pan aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Choose standard or connected.</strong> In a standard group, but=
tons respond to the one that is pressed; a <a href=3D"#components-button-gr=
oup--connected">connected group</a> joins them into one control.</li>
<li><strong>Keep buttons alike.</strong> Use the same size and shape for ev=
ery button, and mix sizes only for hero moments.</li>
<li><strong>Group related buttons.</strong> Mix colors and widths to emphas=
ize what matters and to group related actions.</li>
<li><strong>Let it adapt.</strong> On narrow screens, trailing buttons can =
collapse into an <a href=3D"#components-button-group--overflow-menu">overfl=
ow menu</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>This component is new in <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/blog/building=
-with-m3-expressive">M3 Expressive</a>.</p>
