<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Default</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>density</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">The density of the butt=
ons inside, from 0 (default) to -3. Each step down removes 4px from the but=
tons' height (<a href=3D"http://button-groups.md">button-groups.md</a>: "Bu=
tton groups adapt to the height of the buttons inside, including when densi=
ty is applied"); touch targets stay 48px. A button's own non-zero <code>den=
sity</code> wins. Values are clamped to that range.</span></td>
<td><code>density</code></td>
<td><code>Density</code></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>disabled</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Whether the button gro=
up is disabled.</span></td>
<td><code>disabled</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>overflowMenu</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Whether the button=
s at the trailing edge that do not fit collapse into a trailing overflow me=
nu, and come back when the group has room again (<a href=3D"http://button-g=
roups.md">button-groups.md</a>, Adaptive design: "Buttons at the trailing e=
dge of the button group can be customized to collapse into an overflow menu=
 at smaller breakpoints, and become visible again at larger sizes."). The g=
roup is as wide as its container allows: give it a width, or put it in a na=
rrower container, to make buttons overflow. Choosing a menu entry clicks th=
e original button.</span></td>
<td><code>overflow-menu</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>required</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Whether selection is r=
equired in single-select mode.</span></td>
<td><code>required</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>resizing</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">How the group and its =
buttons resize (<a href=3D"http://button-groups.md">button-groups.md</a>, R=
esizing). <code>fixed</code>: every button keeps the width its own size and=
 width give it. <code>flexible</code>: the group fills the width of its con=
tainer and its buttons grow with it; an icon button does not stretch past i=
ts set width, and a button with <code>resizing=3D"fixed"</code> keeps its w=
idth. A button with <code>resizing=3D"flexible"</code> in a fixed group gro=
ws when the group is given more width. Unset: a connected group is flexible=
 (it spans its surface), a standard group is fixed.</span></td>
<td><code>resizing</code></td>
<td><code>ButtonGroupResizing</code></td>
<td><code>""</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>selection</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">The selection mode.</=
span></td>
<td><code>selection</code></td>
<td><code>ButtonGroupSelection</code></td>
<td><code>"none"</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>variant</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">The visual variant of t=
he button group.</span></td>
<td><code>variant</code></td>
<td><code>ButtonGroupVariant</code></td>
<td><code>"standard"</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
