<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-button--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidel=
ines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-button--usage-guidelines"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Label the action.</strong> A button's text describes what happe=
ns when it is pressed, such as "Save" or "Join now".</li>
<li><strong>Match emphasis to importance.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#componen=
ts-button--colors">filled</a> for the final action of a flow, <a href=3D"#c=
omponents-button--colors">tonal</a> and <a href=3D"#components-button--colo=
rs">outlined</a> for medium emphasis, and <a href=3D"#components-button--co=
lors">text</a> for the lowest priority.</li>
<li><strong>Use elevated sparingly.</strong> Elevated buttons add a shadow,=
 so reserve them for buttons that need separation from a patterned backgrou=
nd.</li>
<li><strong>Add an icon to draw attention.</strong> An <a href=3D"#componen=
ts-button--with-an-icon">icon</a> can help communicate the action.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-button--anatomy" tabindex=3D"-1">Anatomy</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-button--anatomy"><span class=3D"off=
screen">Link to =E2=80=9CAnatomy=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true"=
>#</span></a></div>
<p>A button is one element holding a label and an optional icon (default sl=
ot). It renders a native <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> or, with <code>href</c=
ode>, a link.</p>
