<h2 id=3D"components-button--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</=
h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-button--accessibility"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Buttons need a visible label; add an <a href=3D"https://developer.mozil=
la.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-label"><code>aria-=
label</code></a> to icon-only buttons or when the label needs to be more de=
scriptive.</li>
<li>Buttons activate with Enter and Space and are reachable with Tab.</li>
<li>Disabled buttons leave the tab order. Use <code>soft-disabled</code> to=
 keep one focusable, as the <a href=3D"https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/prac=
tices/keyboard-interface/#kbd_disabled_controls">ARIA guidance on disabled =
controls</a> allows.</li>
<li>Toggle buttons expose their state with <code>aria-pressed</code>.</li>
</ul>
