<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-fab-menu--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility=
</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-fab-menu--accessibility"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-h=
idden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Name the menu with <code>aria-label</code>, such as "Message actions". =
It labels the toggle button.</li>
<li>The toggle button exposes whether the menu is expanded or collapsed.</l=
i>
<li>Tab moves through the button and the items, and Enter or Space activate=
s the focused one.</li>
<li>A menu over scrolling content shouldn't hide focused elements. Register=
 it with <code>setupScrollPadding()</code> from <code>appbar/scroll-padding=
.js</code>.</li>
</ul>
