<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-fab--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guideline=
s</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-fab--usage-guidelines"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>One main action.</strong> Use a FAB for the most important acti=
on on a screen. It floats in front of other content.</li>
<li><strong>Pick a size.</strong> Choose by visual hierarchy: the default F=
AB, a medium FAB (most recommended) or a <a href=3D"#components-fab--sizes"=
>large FAB</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Add a label for emphasis.</strong> An <a href=3D"#components-fa=
b--extended">extended FAB</a> shows a text label next to its icon. It can <=
a href=3D"#components-fab--collapse-on-scroll">collapse</a> while a page sc=
rolls.</li>
<li><strong>Place it consistently.</strong> A FAB can sit at the start, cen=
ter or end, above a navigation bar or nested in it.</li>
</ul>
