<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-icon-button--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage g=
uidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-icon-button--usage-guidelines"><spa=
n class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <sp=
an aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use a clear icon.</strong> Pick a system icon whose meaning peo=
ple already know, and give the button an accessible name that describes the=
 action.</li>
<li><strong>Describe the action on hover.</strong> On the web, add a <a hre=
f=3D"#components-icon-button--tooltip">tooltip</a> so the action is named w=
hile hovering or focusing the button.</li>
<li><strong>Pick the color by emphasis.</strong> <a href=3D"#components-ico=
n-button--colors">Filled</a> is the most prominent, <a href=3D"#components-=
icon-button--colors">tonal</a> and <a href=3D"#components-icon-button--colo=
rs">outlined</a> are medium, and the standard color suits the lowest priori=
ty.</li>
<li><strong>Show state with a toggle.</strong> A <a href=3D"#components-ico=
n-button--toggle">toggle</a> button uses the outlined icon when unselected =
and the filled icon when selected.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
