<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-icon-button--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibil=
ity</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-icon-button--accessibility"><span c=
lass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span ari=
a-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>An icon button has no visible text, so always give it an <a href=3D"htt=
ps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/ari=
a-label"><code>aria-label</code></a> that describes the action.</li>
<li>Icon buttons activate with Enter and Space and are reachable with Tab.<=
/li>
<li>Disabled buttons leave the tab order. Use <code>soft-disabled</code> to=
 keep one focusable, as the <a href=3D"https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/prac=
tices/keyboard-interface/#kbd_disabled_controls">ARIA guidance on disabled =
controls</a> allows.</li>
<li>Toggle buttons expose their state with <code>aria-pressed</code>.</li>
</ul>
