<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-segmented-button--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Us=
age guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-segmented-button--usage-guidelines"=
><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span=
> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Prefer a connected button group.</strong> Material 3 Expressive=
 no longer recommends segmented buttons; the connected <a href=3D"#componen=
ts-button-group">button group</a> has mostly the same function with an upda=
ted look.</li>
<li><strong>Keep it to two to five segments.</strong> For more options or m=
ore complex choices, use <a href=3D"#components-chip">chips</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Pick the selection mode.</strong> A set is <a href=3D"#componen=
ts-segmented-button--examples">single-select</a> by default; add <a href=3D=
"#components-segmented-button--multi-select">multiselect</a> when people ca=
n choose several.</li>
<li><strong>Use icons, labels or both.</strong> Make sure each <a href=3D"#=
components-segmented-button--icons">icon-only</a> segment has an accessible=
 name.</li>
</ul>
