<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-split-button--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage =
guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-split-button--usage-guidelines"><sp=
an class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <s=
pan aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>One main action plus related ones.</strong> The leading button =
runs the most common action, and the menu holds the alternatives.</li>
<li><strong>Same sizes as buttons.</strong> Split buttons come in the five =
button sizes, so they can sit next to <a href=3D"#components-button">button=
s</a> and icon buttons of the same size.</li>
<li><strong>Trailing menu icon.</strong> The trailing button always shows t=
he menu icon. Its color doesn't change when the menu opens; it only turns.<=
/li>
</ul>
