ps://material-web.dev/3.0/r/md-time-picker.json</code> (<a href=3D"#about-s=
hadcn">setup</a>)</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-time-picker--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage g=
uidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-time-picker--usage-guidelines"><spa=
n class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <sp=
an aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Dial or input.</strong> The dial is quick for picking an approx=
imate time, and typing is faster for an exact one. People can <a href=3D"#c=
omponents-time-picker--input-mode">switch</a> between them unless you hide =
the toggle.</li>
<li><strong>Inline or modal.</strong> Show the picker <a href=3D"#component=
s-time-picker--inline-and-modal">inline</a> in a form, or as a <a href=3D"#=
components-time-picker--inline-and-modal">modal</a> when it opens from a fi=
eld or button.</li>
<li><strong>Match the locale.</strong> The picker follows the 12 or 24 hour=
 clock of its <code>locale</code>. Set <a href=3D"#components-time-picker--=
hour-cycle"><code>hour-cycle</code></a> to force one.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-time-picker--anatomy" tabindex=3D"-1">Anatomy</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-time-picker--anatomy"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAnatomy=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<p>A time picker has a headline, the hour and minute selectors, an AM or PM=
 toggle in 12 hour mode, a dial, and the actions.</p>
