ps://material-web.dev/3.0/r/md-loading-indicator.json</code> (<a href=3D"#a=
bout-shadcn">setup</a>)</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-loading-indicator--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">U=
sage guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-loading-indicator--usage-guidelines=
"><span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</spa=
n> <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use it for short waits.</strong> A loading indicator suits proc=
esses that finish in under five seconds, and replaces most uses of an indet=
erminate circular <a href=3D"#components-progress">progress indicator</a>.<=
/li>
<li><strong>Reflect real work.</strong> It always represents an ongoing pro=
cess and is never only decorative.</li>
<li><strong>Don't switch to determinate.</strong> Avoid it for processes th=
at start indeterminate and later report progress; use a progress indicator =
there.</li>
<li><strong>Use it for refreshing.</strong> A <a href=3D"#components-pull-t=
o-refresh">pull to refresh</a> container shows a contained loading indicato=
r.</li>
</ul>
<p>This component is new in <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/blog/building=
-with-m3-expressive">M3 Expressive</a>.</p>
