<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-progress--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guid=
elines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-progress--usage-guidelines"><span c=
lass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span =
aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pick the variant.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-progress-=
-linear">linear</a> for progress across a page or container and <a href=3D"=
#components-progress--circular">circular</a> for a compact spot such as a b=
utton or a card.</li>
<li><strong>Use the same style for the same process.</strong> Keep one conf=
iguration for all the instances of a process, like loading.</li>
<li><strong>Show real progress when you know it.</strong> Set a <a href=3D"=
#components-progress--determinate">value</a> for determinate progress, and =
leave it off when the length of the process is unknown.</li>
<li><strong>Use wavy sparingly.</strong> A <a href=3D"#components-progress-=
-wavy">wavy</a> active indicator is more expressive; use it where that fits=
 your product.</li>
<li><strong>For short waits, use a loading indicator.</strong> The <a href=
=3D"#components-loading-indicator">loading indicator</a> replaces most inde=
terminate circular progress indicators.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-progress--anatomy" tabindex=3D"-1">Anatomy</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-progress--anatomy"><span class=3D"o=
ffscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAnatomy=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"tru=
e">#</span></a></div>
<p>A progress indicator is one element: an active indicator over a track. I=
t is linear unless <code>circular</code> is set.</p>
