<p><strong>Install with shadcn/ui:</strong> <code>npx shadcn@latest add htt=
ps://material-web.dev/3.0/r/md-pull-to-refresh.json</code> (<a href=3D"#abo=
ut-shadcn">setup</a>)</p>
<p>Pull to refresh is the pull-to-refresh behavior of the <a href=3D"#compo=
nents-loading-indicator">loading indicator</a>, which it shows while the co=
ntent reloads.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-pull-to-refresh--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usa=
ge guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-pull-to-refresh--usage-guidelines">=
<span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span>=
 <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Refresh content people expect to change.</strong> Use it on fee=
ds and lists that update, such as news or messages.</li>
<li><strong>Always offer another way.</strong> Pulling isn't available to e=
veryone, so provide a <a href=3D"#components-pull-to-refresh--refresh-butto=
n">refresh button</a> that people can use with a single pointer or the keyb=
oard.</li>
<li><strong>Show it is working.</strong> The container keeps the indicator =
in view until you set <code>refreshing</code> back to <code>false</code>.</=
li>
</ul>
<p>This component is new in <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/blog/building=
-with-m3-expressive">M3 Expressive</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-pull-to-refresh--anatomy" tabindex=3D"-1">Anatomy</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-pull-to-refresh--anatomy"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAnatomy=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=
=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
