<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-navigation-bar--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usag=
e guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-navigation-bar--usage-guidelines"><=
span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> =
<span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use it in compact and medium windows.</strong> From expanded wi=
ndows up, switch to a <a href=3D"#components-navigation-rail">navigation ra=
il</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Keep three to five destinations.</strong> They should be of equ=
al importance.</li>
<li><strong>Keep destinations consistent.</strong> The same destinations ap=
pear on every screen of the app.</li>
<li><strong>Pick the item layout.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-navig=
ation-bar--item-layout">vertical</a> items in compact windows and horizonta=
l items from medium windows.</li>
</ul>
<p>This component is new in <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/blog/building=
-with-m3-expressive">M3 Expressive</a>.</p>
