aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Give the bar an <code>aria-label</code> such as "Primary navigation".</=
li>
<li>Without links the bar is a tab list and its items are tabs, with exactl=
y one selected. Tab moves focus into the bar, the arrow keys move between i=
tems, and Enter and Space select one.</li>
<li>When the items have an <code>href</code> the bar is a navigation landma=
rk of links and the selected one is <code>aria-current=3D"page"</code>. Ent=
er follows a link; Space doesn't.</li>
<li>Every item needs a visible label, which is also its accessible name. If=
 the label is ambiguous, add a more descriptive <code>aria-label</code> to =
the item.</li>
<li>A hidden bar never hides while focus is inside it or when the page scro=
lls from a key press, and it reappears when focus moves into it. Leave <cod=
e>scroll-behavior</code> off if screen reader users rely on the bar.</li>
<li>Disabled items leave the tab order.</li>
</ul>
