<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-navigation-rail--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usa=
ge guidelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-navigation-rail--usage-guidelines">=
<span class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span>=
 <span aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use it in medium windows and larger.</strong> On compact window=
s use a <a href=3D"#components-navigation-bar">navigation bar</a> instead.<=
/li>
<li><strong>Keep three to seven destinations.</strong> Add an optional FAB =
or menu button in the header.</li>
<li><strong>Keep it in the same place.</strong> The rail stays at the leadi=
ng edge on every screen of the app.</li>
<li><strong>Let it expand.</strong> A <a href=3D"#components-navigation-rai=
l--collapsible">collapsed</a> rail shows icons and short labels, and an exp=
anded rail shows horizontal items and can replace a navigation drawer.</li>
</ul>
<p>This component is new in <a href=3D"https://m3.material.io/blog/building=
-with-m3-expressive">M3 Expressive</a>.</p>
