<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-navigation-rail--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Access=
ibility</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-navigation-rail--accessibility"><sp=
an class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span=
 aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Give the rail an <code>aria-label</code> such as "Primary navigation".<=
/li>
<li>Without links the rail is a tab list and its items are tabs, with exact=
ly one selected. Tab moves focus into the rail, the arrow keys move between=
 items, and Enter and Space select one.</li>
<li>When the items have an <code>href</code> the rail is a navigation landm=
ark of links and the selected one is <code>aria-current=3D"page"</code>. En=
ter follows a link; Space doesn't.</li>
<li>Every item needs a visible label, which is also its accessible name.</l=
i>
<li>Give a menu button in the header an <code>aria-label</code>, such as "O=
pen menu".</li>
<li>A modal rail collapses on Escape and when the scrim is pressed. Keep th=
e menu button available as the single-pointer alternative to swiping it clo=
sed.</li>
<li>Disabled items leave the tab order.</li>
</ul>
