l rail is expanded, focus moves into it, Tab stays inside it, page scrollin=
g is locked, and focus returns to the previous element when it collapses. T=
he <code>toggle</code> event's <code>detail.reason</code> says why a modal =
rail collapsed (<code>escape</code>, <code>back</code>, <code>scrim</code> =
or <code>swipe</code>). Predictive back applies to the modal expanded rail =
(<a href=3D"http://navigation-rail.md">navigation-rail.md</a>): while it is=
 expanded the rail listens for back requests with a <code>CloseWatcher</cod=
e> (the Android back gesture or button, and Escape), falling back to Escape=
 on the document where <code>CloseWatcher</code> is missing. A back request=
 plays the predictive back motion (the rail pops off its edge, Compose <cod=
e>ModalWideNavigationRail</code> scales) and collapses the rail. A FAB (<co=
de>md-gb-fab</code> with a <code>label</code>) in the header is an extended=
 FAB while the rail is expanded and an icon FAB while it is collapsed.</td>
