<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-sheets--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidel=
ines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-sheets--usage-guidelines"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Secondary content.</strong> Sheets hold extra content and actio=
ns, not the main content of the app.</li>
<li><strong>Match the window size.</strong> Use a <a href=3D"#components-sh=
eets--bottom-sheets">bottom sheet</a> in compact and medium windows and a <=
a href=3D"#components-sheets--side-sheets">side sheet</a> in wider ones.</l=
i>
<li><strong>Standard or modal.</strong> A standard sheet sits beside the co=
ntent so people can keep using it. A modal sheet blocks the page under a sc=
rim until it is closed.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-sheets--anatomy" tabindex=3D"-1">Anatomy</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-sheets--anatomy"><span class=3D"off=
screen">Link to =E2=80=9CAnatomy=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidden=3D"true"=
>#</span></a></div>
<p>A bottom sheet has a container and an optional drag handle. A side sheet=
 adds a headline, a close button and actions.</p>
