<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
127"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Method</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>close</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">(reason?: string) =3D&gt;=
 Promise&lt;void&gt;</span></td>
<td>Closes the sheet. Resolves after the closing motion.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>expand</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">() =3D&gt; void</span></=
td>
<td>Expands the sheet to its full height.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>handleBack</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">() =3D&gt; Promise&l=
t;void&gt;</span></td>
<td>Handles a back request (the Android back gesture or button, which a mod=
al sheet receives through its dialog): plays the predictive back motion and=
 closes the sheet with reason <code>back</code>. If the <code>close</code> =
event is canceled, the sheet settles back. Resolves after the closing motio=
n. Call it for an in-app back control that should behave like the system ba=
ck.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>partialExpand</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">() =3D&gt; void</=
span></td>
<td>Moves the sheet to its partially expanded height, when it has one.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>render</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">() =3D&gt; TemplateResul=
t&lt;1&gt;</span></td>
<td>Invoked on each update to perform rendering tasks. This method may retu=
rn any value renderable by lit-html's <code>ChildPart</code> - typically a =
<code>TemplateResult</code>. Setting properties inside this method will <em=
>not</em> trigger the element to update.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>show</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">() =3D&gt; Promise&lt;void=
&gt;</span></td>
<td>Opens the sheet. Resolves after the opening motion.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
