<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-app-bar--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guide=
lines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-app-bar--usage-guidelines"><span cl=
ass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span a=
ria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Keep it about the page.</strong> An app bar shows the title, na=
vigation and a few actions that belong to the current page.</li>
<li><strong>Limit the actions.</strong> Show one action, two if needed, and=
 put many actions in a toolbar. Avoid an overflow menu when you can.</li>
<li><strong>Pick a size.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-app-bar--sizes=
">medium or large</a> for a more expressive headline, and a <a href=3D"#com=
ponents-app-bar--sizes">small</a> bar once content scrolls.</li>
