<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-app-bar--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility<=
/h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-app-bar--accessibility"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>The title is the app bar's text, so make it match the page. Add context=
 in an <code>aria-label</code> if the title alone is unclear.</li>
<li>Label every icon-only button with <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
<li>Tab moves through the buttons, and Enter or Space activates the focused=
 one.</li>
<li>A sticky or fixed app bar can cover focused content. Call <code>setupSc=
rollPadding()</code> from <code>scroll-padding.js</code> so focused element=
s scroll clear of it.</li>
</ul>
