<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-badge--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guideli=
nes</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-badge--usage-guidelines"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span ari=
a-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use a dot for something new.</strong> A badge without content s=
ignals new or changed information.</li>
<li><strong>Use a count for a number.</strong> A large badge shows a number=
, such as unread messages.</li>
<li><strong>Keep counts short.</strong> Content is limited to four characte=
rs, including a <code>+</code>, so large numbers show as <code>999+</code>.=
</li>
<li><strong>Attach it to an icon.</strong> <a href=3D"#components-badge--an=
chored">Anchor</a> the badge to the top trailing corner of the icon it desc=
ribes.</li>
</ul>
