<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-card--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</h2=
>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-card--accessibility"><span class=3D=
"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>An interactive card has the button role, or the link role with <code>hr=
ef</code>. Give it an accessible name with <code>aria-label</code> when its=
 content isn't enough.</li>
<li>A card that isn't interactive is a plain container and needs no role. I=
ts actions are focusable on their own.</li>
<li>Hide purely decorative images from assistive technology.</li>
<li>If a card can be dragged, offer a single-pointer alternative such as a =
menu with move and delete actions.</li>
<li>Tab moves to the next card or actionable element, and Enter or Space ac=
tivates it.</li>
</ul>
