<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-checkbox--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guid=
elines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-checkbox--usage-guidelines"><span c=
lass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span =
aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Select from a set.</strong> Use checkboxes when people can pick=
 any number of options from a list, or to turn one option on or off.</li>
<li><strong>Label every checkbox.</strong> The label is the adjacent text, =
and it should say what checking the box does.</li>
<li><strong>Use a parent for a group.</strong> A parent checkbox shows an <=
a href=3D"#indeterminate">indeterminate</a> state when only some of its chi=
ldren are checked.</li>
<li><strong>Don't apply density by default.</strong> Let people opt in to a=
 <a href=3D"#components-checkbox--density">denser layout</a>.</li>
</ul>
