<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-chip--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidelin=
es</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-chip--usage-guidelines"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pick the type by purpose.</strong> <a href=3D"#components-chip-=
-assist-chips">Assist</a> chips are smart actions, <a href=3D"#components-c=
hip--filter-chips">filter</a> chips filter content, <a href=3D"#components-=
chip--input-chips">input</a> chips are information a person entered, and <a=
 href=3D"#components-chip--suggestion-chips">suggestion</a> chips offer dyn=
amic replies or queries.</li>
<li><strong>Show chips as a set.</strong> Unlike buttons, chips appear dyna=
mically as a group, so always place them in a <a href=3D"#components-chip--=
chip-set">chip set</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Elevate only for protection.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#component=
s-chip--assist-chips">elevated</a> chips when they sit on an image or a bus=
y background.</li>
<li><strong>Keep them compact.</strong> Reduce <a href=3D"#components-chip-=
-density">density</a> when space is tight.</li>
</ul>
