<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-chip--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</h2=
>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-chip--accessibility"><span class=3D=
"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>A chip set is a grid of chips: label it with <a href=3D"https://develop=
er.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-label"><co=
de>aria-label</code></a> or <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/=
docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-labelledby"><code>aria-labelled=
by</code></a>.</li>
<li>Add an <code>aria-label</code> to chips whose text needs to be more des=
criptive.</li>
<li>The set is one tab stop; arrow keys, Home and End move between chips, a=
nd Backspace or Delete removes a removable chip.</li>
<li>Disabled chips leave the focus order; use <code>soft-disabled</code> wh=
ere discoverability matters, per the <a href=3D"https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA=
/apg/practices/keyboard-interface/#kbd_disabled_controls">ARIA guidance on =
disabled controls</a>.</li>
</ul>
