"true">#</span></a></div>
<div class=3D"gb-table" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Table =
167"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Default</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>alwaysFullScreen</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Full-screen di=
alogs are for compact windows only (<a href=3D"http://dialogs.md">dialogs.m=
d</a>: use a basic dialog at medium and expanded). So <code>full-screen</co=
de> applies at compact windows and the dialog is a basic dialog above, with=
 the same slots. The host gets <code>adaptive-basic</code> while it falls b=
ack. Set <code>always-full-screen</code> to keep the full-screen variant at=
 every window size.</span></td>
<td><code>always-full-screen</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>closeLabel</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Accessible label of =
the full-screen close icon button.</span></td>
<td><code>close-label</code></td>
<td><code>string</code></td>
<td><code>'Close'</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>fullScreen</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Uses the full-screen=
 variant: the dialog fills the window, with a header holding a close icon b=
utton, the headline and the confirm action. Meant for compact windows; use =
a basic dialog at larger breakpoints.</span></td>
<td><code>full-screen</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>noFocusTrap</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Turns off focus tra=
pping, which keeps Tab and Shift+Tab cycling inside the dialog. Trapping is=
 recommended for accessibility.</span></td>
<td><code>no-focus-trap</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>open</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Opens the dialog when set =
to <code>true</code> and closes it when set to <code>false</code>.</span></=
td>
<td><code>open</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>quick</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">Skips the opening and clo=
sing animations.</span></td>
<td><code>quick</code></td>
<td><code>boolean</code></td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>returnValue</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">The dialog's return=
 value, usually which button closed it. Set by <code>close(returnValue)</co=
de> and by <code>&lt;form method=3D"dialog"&gt;</code> submitters' <code>va=
lue</code>. Canceling (Escape, scrim, close button) leaves it unchanged. <a=
 href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLDialogElement=
/returnValue">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLDialogEl=
ement/returnValue</a></span></td>
<td></td>
<td><code>string</code></td>
<td><code>''</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>type</code><br><span class=3D"gb-desc">The dialog's accessibility=
 role. <code>alert</code> (<code>role=3D"alertdialog"</code>) or <code>dial=
og</code> (<code>role=3D"dialog"</code>). When empty, basic dialogs are ale=
rt dialogs, as the spec asks for on the web, and full-screen dialogs are di=
alogs.</span></td>
<td><code>type</code></td>
<td><code>DialogType</code></td>
<td><code>''</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"heading h4">
