<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-divider--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guide=
lines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-divider--usage-guidelines"><span cl=
ass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span a=
ria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Group and create hierarchy.</strong> Dividers visually group co=
mponents and can imply a parent and child relationship.</li>
<li><strong>Full width for sections.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-di=
vider--insets">full-width</a> dividers to separate larger sections of unrel=
ated content.</li>
<li><strong>Inset for related items.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-di=
vider--insets">inset dividers</a> to separate related content within a sect=
ion, such as items in a list.</li>
<li><strong>Don't overuse.</strong> Spacing and type styles often separate =
content well enough on their own.</li>
</ul>
