<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-list--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidelin=
es</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-list--usage-guidelines"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Make items easy to scan.</strong> Keep labels short, order item=
s in a logical way such as alphabetical or numerical, and show icons, text =
and actions in a consistent format.</li>
<li><strong>Choose a style.</strong> A standard list is flat; a <a href=3D"=
#components-list--segmented">segmented</a> list separates each item into it=
s own container.</li>
<li><strong>Match the item to its content.</strong> Add <a href=3D"#compone=
nts-list--slots">supporting text</a>, an overline, an avatar or a leading i=
con to describe what an item is.</li>
<li><strong>Add behavior when it helps.</strong> Lists can <a href=3D"#comp=
onents-list--selection">select</a>, <a href=3D"#components-list--reordering=
">reorder</a>, <a href=3D"#components-list--expandable-items">expand</a> an=
d reveal <a href=3D"#components-list--swipe-actions">swipe actions</a>.</li=
>
</ul>
