<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-menu--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidelin=
es</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-menu--usage-guidelines"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use it for temporary actions.</strong> A menu shows a short set=
 of actions on demand. To show actions on screen at all times, use a <a hre=
f=3D"#components-toolbar">toolbar</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Open it from many places.</strong> A menu can open from a butto=
n, an icon button, a split button or a text field, or as a <a href=3D"#comp=
onents-menu--context-menu">context menu</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Organize long menus.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-menu--=
groups">groups</a> with labels and dividers to separate related choices.</l=
i>
<li><strong>Choose a color.</strong> The <code>standard</code> color suits =
most menus; <code>vibrant</code> makes the selected items stand out.</li>
</ul>
