<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-radio--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guideli=
nes</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-radio--usage-guidelines"><span clas=
s=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span ari=
a-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use radios for a single choice.</strong> Pick radio buttons, no=
t switches, when only one option can be selected from a list; use checkboxe=
s when several can.</li>
<li><strong>Show every option.</strong> Radios expose all the choices, so u=
se them for five or fewer; consider a menu when space is tight.</li>
<li><strong>Always add a label.</strong> Each radio needs its own scannable=
 label, and a person can select either the radio or its label.</li>
<li><strong>Preselect one and stack them.</strong> List radios vertically w=
ith one option already selected, and avoid nesting them.</li>
</ul>
