<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-radio--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</h=
2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-radio--accessibility"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Place radios in a <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/W=
eb/Accessibility/ARIA/Roles/radiogroup_role"><code>role=3D"radiogroup"</cod=
e></a> and label the group with <code>aria-label</code> or <code>aria-label=
ledby</code>.</li>
<li>Name each radio with a <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code> that points at it=
s <code>id</code>. Use an <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/do=
cs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-label"><code>aria-label</code></a=
> only for a radio with no visible label.</li>
<li>Don't wrap a radio in its <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>; screen readers th=
en can't announce the number of radios in the group.</li>
<li>Tab moves focus to the selected radio of a group, and the arrow keys mo=
ve the selection between radios. Space selects the focused radio.</li>
<li>Once a radio is selected the group can't be cleared, so add a "None" op=
tion or a "Clear selection" control if people may opt out.</li>
</ul>
