<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-select--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidel=
ines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-select--usage-guidelines"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fixed list of choices.</strong> Use a select to choose one valu=
e from a short, fixed list, like the native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>. Fo=
r a longer list that people can search, use the <a href=3D"#components-sele=
ct--autocomplete">autocomplete</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Pick the variant by emphasis.</strong> Filled selects stand out=
 more; <a href=3D"#components-select--variants">outlined</a> selects are li=
ghter on dense forms.</li>
<li><strong>Say what is wrong.</strong> Pair an <a href=3D"#components-sele=
ct--error-and-supporting-text">error</a> with text that explains how to fix=
 it.</li>
</ul>
