<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-snackbar--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guid=
elines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-snackbar--usage-guidelines"><span c=
lass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span =
aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Low priority only.</strong> Use a snackbar for a message that n=
eeds no response. For an important one that blocks the task, use a dialog.<=
/li>
<li><strong>One at a time.</strong> Show a single snackbar, and queue <a hr=
ef=3D"#components-snackbar--consecutive-snackbars">consecutive</a> messages=
.</li>
<li><strong>At most one action.</strong> Give it a short action such as Und=
o. A snackbar with an action stays until it is used or dismissed.</li>
<li><strong>Repeat the message nearby.</strong> A snackbar that disappears =
on its own is easy to miss, so also show the result inline, such as changin=
g "Save" to "Saved".</li>
</ul>
