<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-switch--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidel=
ines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-switch--usage-guidelines"><span cla=
ss=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use for settings.</strong> Switches are the best way to let peo=
ple adjust a setting. Use a switch, not a radio button, when each item in a=
 list is controlled on its own.</li>
<li><strong>Visible at a glance.</strong> Make the on or off state clear, a=
nd let the change take effect right away.</li>
<li><strong>Label with text.</strong> Put the label next to the switch in a=
 <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>. Its text color stays the same, even when the s=
witch changes.</li>
</ul>
