<h2 id=3D"components-tabs--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guidelin=
es</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-tabs--usage-guidelines"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria=
-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Same level of hierarchy.</strong> Tabs switch between views of =
related content that are peers. Don't use them for steps in a flow.</li>
<li><strong>Primary or secondary.</strong> <a href=3D"#components-tabs--pri=
mary-and-secondary">Primary</a> tabs sit at the top of the content under a =
top app bar and show the main destinations. <a href=3D"#components-tabs--pr=
imary-and-secondary">Secondary</a> tabs split a content area further. Use o=
ne type in a bar.</li>
<li><strong>Short labels.</strong> Keep labels to a word or two. Use <a hre=
f=3D"#components-tabs--icons">icons</a> only when they are simple and recog=
nizable.</li>
<li><strong>Avoid dense tabs by default.</strong> Lowering the <a href=3D"#=
components-tabs--density">density</a> shrinks the targets below 48px, so le=
t people opt in.</li>
</ul>
