<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-tabs--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility</h2=
>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-tabs--accessibility"><span class=3D=
"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hidde=
n=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>Tabs use the <code>tablist</code>, <code>tab</code> and <code>tabpanel<=
/code> roles. Label the tab list with <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.=
org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-label"><code>aria-lab=
el</code></a> or <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Ac=
cessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-labelledby"><code>aria-labelledby</code></=
a>, and give icon-only tabs an <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
<li>The list is one tab stop. The arrow keys move between tabs, and Space o=
r Enter selects the focused one.</li>
<li>Each tab controls a panel, and each panel is labelled by its tab. Linki=
ng them with <code>tabpanel</code> or <code>md-gb-tab-panels</code> does th=
is for you.</li>
</ul>
