<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-text-field--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage gu=
idelines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-text-field--usage-guidelines"><span=
 class=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <spa=
n aria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Filled or outlined.</strong> Filled fields have more visual wei=
ght and suit most forms. <a href=3D"#components-text-field--variants">Outli=
ned</a> fields are lighter and work where many fields sit together. Don't m=
ix them in one form.</li>
<li><strong>Label every field.</strong> The label floats above the text onc=
e the field has a value or focus. Use a <a href=3D"#components-text-field--=
variants">placeholder</a> only as an example of the input, never in place o=
f the label.</li>
<li><strong>Help before and after.</strong> Use <a href=3D"#components-text=
-field--supporting-text-and-counter">supporting text</a> for hints, and exp=
lain what went wrong in an <a href=3D"#components-text-field--error-and-val=
idation">error</a>.</li>
</ul>
