<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-toolbar--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guide=
lines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-toolbar--usage-guidelines"><span cl=
ass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span a=
ria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Actions for the page.</strong> A toolbar offers actions related=
 to the current page and can show more of them in larger windows.</li>
<li><strong>Docked or floating.</strong> A <a href=3D"#components-toolbar--=
docked">docked</a> toolbar spans the window and suits global actions that s=
tay the same across pages. A floating toolbar hovers over the content and s=
uits actions for that content.</li>
<li><strong>Vibrant for emphasis.</strong> Use the <a href=3D"#components-t=
oolbar--colors">vibrant</a> color for more emphasis.</li>
<li><strong>Not with a navigation bar.</strong> Don't show a toolbar at the=
 same time as a navigation bar.</li>
</ul>
