<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-toolbar--accessibility" tabindex=3D"-1">Accessibility<=
/h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-toolbar--accessibility"><span class=
=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CAccessibility=E2=80=9D</span> <span aria-hi=
dden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li>A toolbar has the <code>toolbar</code> role. Label it with <a href=3D"h=
ttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/a=
ria-label"><code>aria-label</code></a> or <a href=3D"https://developer.mozi=
lla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes/aria-labelledby"><code=
>aria-labelledby</code></a>.</li>
<li>Every action stays in the Tab order, and the arrow keys also move betwe=
en them (up and down in a vertical toolbar).</li>
<li>Icon-only actions need an <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
<li>A collapsed toolbar makes its hidden actions inert.</li>
</ul>
