<div class=3D"heading h2">
<h2 id=3D"components-tooltip--usage-guidelines" tabindex=3D"-1">Usage guide=
lines</h2>
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"#components-tooltip--usage-guidelines"><span cl=
ass=3D"offscreen">Link to =E2=80=9CUsage guidelines=E2=80=9D</span> <span a=
ria-hidden=3D"true">#</span></a></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Plain to label.</strong> Use a <a href=3D"#components-tooltip--=
placement">plain</a> tooltip to name an element with no text, such as an ic=
on-only button. Don't add one when the element already has a visible label.=
</li>
<li><strong>Rich for details.</strong> Use a <a href=3D"#components-tooltip=
--rich">rich</a> tooltip for longer text, such as a definition or an explan=
ation of a new feature, with an optional subhead and up to two text buttons=
.</li>
<li><strong>Nothing critical.</strong> Tooltips are easy to miss, so never =
hide information people must see. Use a dialog for that.</li>
</ul>
